  "Scenes.Marielle.MeetStayPut.FearfulReaction": "Quite a fearful reaction. You don't provoke it any further, and instead remain sitting still. {0} how this girl is still breathing, despite her corpse-like appearance. When you make it clear that you aren't going to cause her any harm, she lets go of a held breath in form of a sigh and faintly nods to herself, her shoulders and entire posture releasing the tension they held. One hand remains loosely rested on the guard of her longsword, though."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MeetStayPut.VoiceFailsAgain": "[pg][say:Well, I--] Her voice abruptly fails her again, and she hurries for another swig of water before trying anew. [say:I suppose I must thank you once more for your kindness...] [if (corruption < 40) {You wonder why she would feel the need to thank you for that, but keep that question to yourself.|You're not so sure about that 'kindness' part, but don't say anything.}] She isn't looking at you any longer anyway, but has instead lost herself deep inside the puddle, her face contorting into a dismayed frown at what she finds."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MeetSword.ExpressionUnchanged": "[pg]The girl's expression hasn't changed a bit when you glance back at her, though now she has two eyes to glare daggers at you with."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MeetSword.IncredulousPanic": "[pg][say:My blade?] she says, incredulous for a second before panic grips her. [say:But-- But 'tis the only one I possess! Surely would you bereave me not of my sole guardian?] She heard you the first time, the deal is her sword for her eye, and you make that clear."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MeetSword.NiceEngravedLongsword": "[pg]It's a pretty nice longsword, beautifully engraved with birds and flowers, and it feels quite light and nimble in your hands; hardly a bother to swing--she probably chose it for that very reason. Well, it's yours now."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MeetSword.NicestSendOff": "[pg]Not the nicest of send-offs, but you hardly expected better. As you make your way out of the temple and towards your campsite, you doubt you'll ever see that girl again."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MeetSword.SpitsCurseBanditry": "[pg][say:For your aid, I thank you, but for your dastard banditry, I wish rot and malady upon thee,] she all but spits, balling her hands to fists and jerking away from you. [say:Now get thee gone, wretch.]"
  "Scenes.Marielle.MeetSword.TakesHerSword": "You tell her you'll take her sword."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MeetSword.TriesTrailsOff": "[pg][say:But...] she tries once more but trails off, evidently giving up. As she stares down at the handle for a long moment, her features contort into a glower, but she finally unties the bow of her sash, yanks the scabbard out of its fastening loops, and wordlessly thrusts it towards you, a look of sheer resentment on her face. If she didn't just surrender you her weapon, you'd be worried she'd try and murder you regardless of her feeble condition. You hand over the eye in exchange, then turn to marvel at the sword you just extorted."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MothCommissionBack.NotGetAnything": "You choose to not get anything right now, a decision that is met with a quiet [say:Hmm] as Marielle gives you back the bundle of silk."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MothCommissions.AdjustsSpectaclesRepeat": "more than once adjusting her round spectacles to have a closer look at something in particular."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MothCommissions.BringsToFace": "bringing it to her face for the occasional closer look. Though gradually, that intrigued expression makes way for a different one--a frown that spells a question brewing in her mind. It culminates in her finally half-canting towards you."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MothCommissions.DepositIntoHands": "[pg][say:Oh, pray allow me.] Depositing it into Marielle's outstretched hands, you let her examine the bundle of white, near-pristine fibers with careful motions. She does find quite some interest in it, running her fingertips along the torn edges, picking off little specks of dirt, and "
  "Scenes.Marielle.MothCommissions.GoodSilkIndeed": "[pg][say:...Well, 'tis good silk indeed; right magnific, even,] she informs you while stretching it out against the light of her lantern. [say:Whiles enriven the filament may be, its, ah, size alone ought yet furnish adequate material for even a gown, I ween...] The girl scrutinizes it for a moment longer before setting everything down and turning to you."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MothCommissions.ItIsDaughters": "[pg][say:If... 'moth', you say, mean you...?] It's your daughter's, you elaborate, from her cocoon, to be exact. [say:O-Oh. I... see.] Marielle seems reasonably flustered by that piece of knowledge, holding the thing now even more gingerly."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MothCommissions.LargeMothSilkPiece": "You have a pretty large piece of moth-silk here, courtesy of Dolores. You unpack it and ask the seamstress if she can make anything from it."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MothCommissions.MothSayYou": "[pg][say:'Moth', say you?] the seamstress eventually asks, her eyes remaining on the silk. You elaborate a little, telling her it's your very own daughter's, and that you're free to do with it whatever you want."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MothCommissions.NeitherNoticed": "[pg][say:Should that be, ah... all right, then, forsooth? That I put it to scissor, loom, and needle?] Neither Sylvia nor Dolores seemed to really mind what exactly you'd do with it, you tell the seamstress. [say:Oh. Hmm... is that so.] Perhaps somewhat let down, but sufficiently allayed, she nudges her spectacles and goes back to her observation."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MothCommissions.NoCommentButHovering": "[pg][say:Oh. Hmm, I see, I see...] No other comment comes, but you do notice that she's holding the cocoon even more gently now."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MothCommissions.RecognizesSilk": "[pg][say:Ah, yes,] she says, recognizing it. [say:Are you decided what you wish I fashion herefrom?]"
  "Scenes.Marielle.MothCommissions.UnpackCocoonSilk": "You unpack the large bundle of your daughter's cocoon-silk and hand it to Marielle for her scrutiny."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MothCommissions.WhatFashionTherefrom": "[pg][say:So, what wish you I fashion therefrom?]"
  "Scenes.Marielle.MutualWash.AwkwardFailure": "[pg]Well, that was a failure and has only made it awkward for the both of you. You sink further into the pond again and try to let your thoughts stray elsewhere."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MutualWash.BringsAttentionBack": "[pg][say:Hmm?] says the wool-gathering seamstress as you bring her attention back to you by vocalizing your idea of helping each other out. She seems to space out again, momentarily phasing right through you before focussing again."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MutualWash.EyesDriftAside": "[pg][say:I, ah... uhm.] Her eyes drift to the side."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MutualWash.MumblesSoap": "[pg][say:Uhm... Soap, soap... we shall need...] comes from her, more audibly. Happy to have found an excuse to swirl around, Marielle proceeds to fish through the thick towel she brought for herself, by doing so presenting you the tantalizing view of her naked, dripping butt and lower lips suspended just above the waterline."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MutualWash.PullsFromWoolGathering": "[pg][say:Huh?] says the seamstress as you pull her out of her wool-gathering by vocalizing your idea of helping each other out. At your words, her eyes flit down towards your crotch for a split-second, an uneasy shadow casting itself over her pale features, then they seem to avoid you entirely."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MutualWash.RiseExposesChest": "[pg]However, as your rise out of the water exposes your [chest] to the fresh air {0} her head away from your approaching nude, glistening form, and you hear her mumble something unintelligible while she searches[if (femininity >= 69) {{ in desperation}}] for [if (femininity > 50) {{anything else to look at|a means to preserve some modesty}}]."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MutualWash.ShiftsUncomfortably": "[pg][say:I, ah...] Marielle shifts uncomfortably. [say:I would much rather... do so by mine own, [name],] she says, shutting down the plans you had. [say:My apologies... I mean neither insult nor discourtesy, but, ah, well...] She never finishes the sentence, but you think you can figure out the gist of it."
  "Scenes.Marielle.MutualWash.SomeoneElseHere": "Washing yourself is all fine and good, but right now, you've got someone else here with you. And that someone has a lot of hands that you wouldn't mind letting roam over your [skindesc]."
