  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopBalletWatch.SoundsUnsure": "[pg][if (femininity >= 59) {[say:...Be that... all?] She sounds unsure, perhaps having expected you to do more than watch. Well,|[say:...Be you... satisfied, [name]?] She seems eager to go back to business, but}] you're not done quite yet. You shift into a more comfortable sitting position, let yourself relax, and give a contented sigh. A cup of tea, and you'd be in heaven. Sadly, the lone kettle you spot perched atop a stack of boxes appears to be empty. Well, you'll have to do without."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopBalletYes.BeNotAfeard": "[pg][say:Be not afeard to ask, if aught be amiss. I shall be more than glad to make further adjustments.]"
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopBalletYes.ClaspsManyHands": "[say:Oh, wonderful!] Marielle exclaims, clasping her many hands over the offered bundle of gems. [say:Just pray allow me set down your measurements, lest it be not the height of absoluteness and excellence!] You let her take your sizes as she happily hums to herself and gets to work. [say:'Twill but take a moment, fret not.]"
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopBalletYes.PredictionProvesRight": "[pg]Her prediction proves right, and she soon calls you over again to present you the frilly dress with a wide smile."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButler.ChimesInForgotten": "[pg][say:Oh, yes,] Marielle chimes in. [say:Nighly had I forgotten those were yet by my possession...] She takes a cursory glance over what you pulled out, then tacitly indicates in succession a pair of white silk gloves, some suspenders, as well as a bow- and necktie."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButler.FiveEightyGems": "[pg][say:Hmm... 580 gems for the entire livery is what I can offer you.]"
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButler.NotMensSpeciality": "[pg][say:Men's garments are no, ah, speciality of mine, yet once custom-tailored I a few for a client erstwhile who then... vanished thenceafter, with not a word nor note behind. As if into the very air. And never learned I what befell the gentleman.] She adjusts her pince-nez. [say:Well, be that as it may. 'Tis meant for a manservant--a butler--but one may wear it unto any occasion, of import or not. I doubt any one soul here in Mareth would mark the difference...]"
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButler.NoticeButlerPieces": "You notice several pieces that you think belong together: a white shirt, a vest, suit pants, and a tailcoat."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButler.SuitForAnyone": "[pg]The suit does indeed look like it could be worn by just about anyone wanting to look fancy."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButler.TakeItQuestion": "[pg]Do you take it?"
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerModel.BlinksConfused": "Marielle blinks at you, confused."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerModel.HesitantButTakes": "[pg][say:Well... if that be what you wish...] She looks hesitant, but still takes the clothes from you and turns around to change. Her motions are quick, letting you catch only a glimpse of her naked butt before she puts on and fastens the pants."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerModel.SurprisingFit": "[pg]When she turns around, you find it's a surprisingly good fit on her. It does straighten out her figure a bit further, granting the girl a strain of androgyny, but conversely puts the appeal of her fair face, blonde hair, and genteel posture into an even brighter limelight. Though still, the outfit's a tad large; the tailcoat's flaps reach past her knees, and those pants are too slack. And somehow, she managed to squeeze all four arms through the sleeves. She also went for the necktie, not the bow. Maybe she's actually aware of how well it suits her. All in all, it looks as elegant and tasteful as you expected."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerModel.ThinkBuyingIt": "[pg]What do you think indeed; are you buying it?"
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerModel.WellWhatThink": "[pg][say:Well? What think you?]"
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerModel.WishMeDon": "[pg][say:You wish me don... [b:this]?] she asks, and you answer in the affirmative. [say:...Man I am none, neither gentle nor base--that slipped your mind not, yes?] You know, but you still want her to try it on. A sigh escapes her at that."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerModel.YetAgainFrowns": "[say:Yet again?] Marielle frowns, evidently not too keen on modelling the suit."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerModelNo.ChangeOfHeart": "[pg][say:Well, if you chance upon a change of heart, I believe these ones, ah... will depart from my selection not any time soon.]"
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerModelNo.SighsChangesBack": "[say:Hmm, I see...] she sighs and quickly changes back to her usual summer dress."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerModelYes.AlreadyChanging": "[pg][say:Ah, marvellous!] Marielle exclaims, already in the process of changing again. She pulls out a pair of measuring tapes when she's done and says, [say:A couple of, ah, alterations 'twill require, but I will do so apace. Please you, keep still for but a moment...] She's quick to note down your sizes before getting to work."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerModelYes.BuysThisOne": "You'll buy this one."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerModelYes.NoteOvertight": "[pg][say:Ah, give note if aught be... overtight anywhere.]"
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerModelYes.PromisedBeckons": "[pg]As promised, you soon hear her voice beckon you over to her tent again, where she presents you the tailored suit, neatly folded in her arms. You take it and hand over the money in turn after a brief check."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerModelYes.ShallCallFinished": "[pg][say:By and by. I shall call, once 'tis finished,] the seamstress tells you, leaving you to wander the temple for a bit."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerNo.FoldNeatlyBack": "You fold it neatly before putting the pieces back into the chest."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerYes.BespokeIndeed": "[pg][say:Well, 'bespoke' is what it should be indeed, now. But pray tell me if aught be... pinching you.]"
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerYes.HumsContented": "[pg]After a while, she hums a contented [say:Hmmn] and gets up to return the pieces to you."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopButlerYes.MarvellousWillAdjust": "[say:Oh, marvellous,] Marielle says with a smile as you offer her the gems, [say:but I will needs make a few adjustments for you.] She pulls out two measuring tapes and quickly notes your sizes before taking the suit from you and sitting down at her desk."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopCheer.HesitantButContinues": "[pg][say:Ah.] Marielle looks somewhat hesitant, but continues, [say:Well, that is... something I made on... behest, yes, quite a long while agone.] She doesn't seem to be inclined to tell you who commissioned the thing, nor why she's still holding onto it. Instead, she looks like she's searching for something. Standing up and walking over to another pile of boxes, she rummages through them until she pulls out two large, bushy balls and hands them to you before sitting down again. You're not sure what to do with these, but they seem to somewhat fit with the rest of the set, color-wise. Perhaps you're supposed to wave them around, or maybe throw them; if anything, they should be a decent distraction."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopCheer.ReallyWantThis": "[pg]Do you really want this?"
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopCheer.StrikingClothingSet": "You fish out a striking set of clothing that was buried near the bottom of the chest: a short skirt and a sleeveless top, both pink and white in color and leaving the wearer's midriff and thighs exposed. This doesn't exactly look like something you'd have expected to be in her inventory."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopCheer.TwoHundredGems": "[pg][say:Well, ah... 200 gems and it shall all be yours, wish you so.]"
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopCheerModel.BuyItRegardless": "[pg]Would you buy it regardless?"
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopCheerModel.FirmRejection": "[pg]That was a fairly firm rejection. As much fun as it would be to see her in this rather revealing set, you doubt she'll let herself be persuaded, here."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopCheerModel.HandGesturesAround": "[pg][say:Well, 'tis, ah...] A single hand loosely gestures around the showy and showing outfit as the seamstress visibly grasps for the right words, almost despairing over them, until a sigh unseals her lips. [say:'Tis much too unseemly. My apologies, [name], but I must refuse you. If there be aught else I may assist you with, then pray tell, but this I shall don not.]"
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopCheerModel.VoicePetersOut": "[say:Oh, I, ah...] She lets her voice peter out to consider, though her expression already tells you that whatever she's going to say next won't be too favorable. [say:I would rather... not.] She won't model that for you? You can guess why, but still ask."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopCheerNo.ReturnFuzzyBalls": "You return the fuzzy balls and stow the top and skirt back into the chest."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopCheerYes.BeckonsWithOutfit": "[pg]Not long after, she beckons you back and gives you the tailored outfit."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopCheerYes.DoubtOrJudgement": "[pg][say:Oh? Oh, you... do?] An expression of doubt--or judgement?--flits over her face before she can expel it and hastily take the offered money with a smile. [say:I, ah, will needs make a few simple alterations aforehand.] She pulls a pair of measuring tapes from the table and moves over to you. [say:Hold you still, please.] You let her note down your sizes and give her some time to work."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopCheerYes.ExcuseYouPomPom": "[pg][say:'Pom-pom'.] Excuse you? [say:Uhm, 'pom-poms', 'tis their, ah, name,] Marielle says as she turns back to you. By way of proof, she presents you the stack of designs she found. The topmost one is a detailed depiction of one such ball in question, complete with illustrations on how exactly it's made. And true enough, underneath it stands in swirly handwriting: 'Pom-Pom', beneath which is then a small series of drawings of a curvy woman doing various athletic poses with two of those in hand."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopCheerYes.EyebrowsPullTogether": "[pg][say:Oh, uhm...] Her eyebrows pull closer together, and she seems to be racking her brain for a while, but doesn't arrive anywhere. So, she turns to the notes she keeps on her desk. But they, too, apparently give no answer to your question, and the increasingly absorbed seamstress starts skimming over her crates until she finds the right one and sifts through its contents. You hear the rustling of paper on paper before a soft [say:Ah] marks her success."
  "Scenes.Marielle.ShopCheerYes.IfPinchSaySo": "[pg][say:Well, that should be all. If it yet pinch you, pray say so, and I shall correct it.]"
